#35301
Limla Cliffs~
   The creek bed slopes down from the east and turns sharply south here,
for the storm waters that rush through have cut into the side of a
gigantic rock wall, and the rock has held firm, forcing the creek aside.
A shallow, stagnant pool about fifteen feet across lies between you and
the cliff, and the air above it is close and heavy.
